msgid ""
"Computational diagnostics are unavailable for this cached fit. Refit the "
"analysis before relying on its decisions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Computational diagnostics could not be calculated. The posterior draws are "
"retained, but computational reliability has not been assessed. Refit the "
"analysis and inspect the sampler output."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Only %1$d of %2$d requested chains are available. Inspect the sampler output "
"for failed chains and refit before relying on the results."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Thinning is enabled. Divergence and treedepth counts cover only retained "
"transitions, so other events may be missed; E-BFMI is unavailable. Rerun "
"with Thinning = 1 for complete sampler checks."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sampler diagnostics are unavailable for one or more chains. Missing checks "
"are not evidence of successful sampling; refit and inspect the sampler "
"output."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Detected %1$d divergent transitions in the available retained post-warmup "
"records. Estimates may be biased. Review the model, priors and sampler "
"settings before relying on the results; increasing Adapt delta may help. No "
"divergent draws were removed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The maximum treedepth was reached in %1$d retained post-warmup iterations. "
"This can reduce sampling efficiency. Inspect mixing and the model before "
"considering a higher treedepth limit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Only one chain was run, so between-chain mixing cannot be assessed and "
"automatic R-hat is unavailable. Run multiple chains, preferably at least "
"four."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fewer than six post-warmup draws per chain are available. R-hat, effective "
"sample sizes and E-BFMI cannot be assessed reliably. Increase the number of "
"retained samples."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At least one chain is constant for %1$d sampled parameter(s), including "
"%2$s. Mixing and effective sample sizes are unavailable for these "
"parameters. Inspect the chains and refit before relying on the results."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Non-finite draws occur in sampled parameters. Their mixing and effective "
"sample sizes are unavailable; investigate the model and sampler output "
"before using the results."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The maximum rank-normalized split R-hat is %1$.3f (%2$s), at or above 1.01. "
"The chains may not have mixed. Inspect their traces, run longer chains, and "
"review the model if the problem persists."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"R-hat is unavailable for one or more sampled parameters. Inspect the chains "
"and refit; this is not a successful mixing check."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bulk or tail effective sample size is below %1$d (100 times the number of "
"chains) for one or more sampled parameters. Monte Carlo estimates may be "
"imprecise. If the chains mix well, increase the number of retained samples; "
"otherwise investigate mixing first."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bulk or tail effective sample size is unavailable for one or more sampled "
"parameters. Inspect the chains and obtain more usable draws before relying "
"on the results."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"E-BFMI is below 0.3 in chain(s) %1$s, indicating poor exploration of the "
"energy distribution. Review the model and priors and consider longer warmup "
"before relying on the results."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"E-BFMI is unavailable for one or more chains because their energy "
"diagnostics are missing, non-finite or constant. Refit with usable energy "
"diagnostics; missing values are not a successful check."
msgstr ""

